From d161b41e629be2d7a037aaf08af89c1da40f27a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 23:09:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] code-review tail (batch A): dead code, redundant work, one
 fork removed

Mechanical items from CODE-REVIEW-2026-08-18, each re-verified reachable at
HEAD before the edit; no behavioural change intended.
- httpd/reaper_inject.c: the three nvram reads (reaper_inject, re_mode,
  disable_ui) ran on EVERY request before the free mime/extension tests;
  now evaluated only for injectable pages. Query string stripped once
  (reaper_page_ext takes the stripped name); over-long names still never
  injected.
- rc/reaper_fw.c: dead rfw_cfg_t.confirm field (rfw_confirm_secs() reads
  nvram directly); stype4/stype6 always identical -> one stype.
- rc/rexport.c: unreachable `mins < 1` clamp (iv>0 forces mins>=1).
- rtrafd/rtrafd.c: struct fcf .dip/.dport were write-only; dst still
  parsed for line validation.
- rmcpd/rmcpd.c: get_overview meminfo via in-process sb_addfile_lines()
  instead of a `grep -E` fork; output byte-identical (file order, newlines,
  256-byte cap).
- www: Reaper_VPNRouting.asp uses the shared esc() from reaper_util.js
  (last local copy); Reaper_Traffic.asp stackChart() drops its unused
  `labels` param; Reaper_FirstBoot.asp drops a shadowed $() redeclaration.
